---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
const title = 'Terms of Use | Proof to Partner';
const description = 'Preliminary terms covering website use, enquiry submissions, commercial introductions, due diligence and the absence of guaranteed outcomes.';
const breadcrumbs = [{ name: 'Home', path: '/' }, { name: 'Terms of use', path: '/terms/' }];
---
<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms/" breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}>
<section class="border-b border-line bg-white py-14 sm:py-20"><div class="container-shell max-w-4xl"><p class="eyebrow">Using this website</p><h1 class="display-heading mt-5 text-5xl font-semibold sm:text-6xl">Terms of Use</h1><p class="mt-5 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: 22 October 2026</p><p class="prose-copy mt-7 text-lg">These preliminary terms describe the intended use of the Proof to Partner website and enquiry process. Review them for the operator's actual legal identity, location and applicable law before launch.</p></div></section>
<section class="section-space"><article class="container-shell max-w-4xl space-y-10">
<aside class="review-note"><h2 class="font-bold">Site owner review required before launch</h2><p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-6">Add the responsible legal entity or individual, a valid contact route and a governing-law/jurisdiction clause after obtaining appropriate advice. This is a preliminary draft and not a substitute for legal review.</p></aside>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">1. Purpose of the website</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Proof to Partner provides information about a developing, cross-industry business-introduction approach. Visitors can submit a commercial requirement, describe supplier capabilities or make a general enquiry. The website is not an open marketplace, procurement platform, professional-advice service or guarantee of a commercial result.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">2. Enquiry submissions</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Provide information that is accurate to the best of your knowledge, that you are authorised to disclose and that is relevant to your enquiry. Do not submit unlawful content, credentials, payment data or confidential third-party information you have no right to share. Submission does not oblige Proof to Partner to accept or fulfil a request.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">3. No guarantee of introductions or outcomes</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">An enquiry may lead to a clarifying question, research, a proposed introduction or no further action. Proof to Partner does not guarantee that a suitable counterpart exists, is available, has stated capabilities, is interested or will enter into an agreement. Any response timeframe is an operational aim, not a contractual service level.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">4. Independent businesses and due diligence</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Potential buyers and suppliers are independent businesses. Unless a separate written agreement expressly says otherwise, an introduction does not mean Proof to Partner employs, represents, endorses, certifies or guarantees either party. Each party is responsible for its own checks, including identity, qualifications, compliance, insurance, financial standing, contract terms and suitability.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">5. Fees and commercial arrangements</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Submitting an enquiry does not itself create a fee or payment obligation. Any finder’s fee, referral fee, service fee, success fee or other arrangement must be explained and expressly agreed by the relevant parties before the related work or introduction proceeds. No pricing is promised by these terms.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">6. Website content and availability</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Content is provided for general informational purposes and may change without notice. Reasonable care is taken with published information, but it may be incomplete or out of date. The website may be unavailable or affected by technical issues, and electronic submission does not guarantee immediate personal review.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">7. Intellectual property and acceptable use</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Unless stated otherwise, the website's original text, visual identity and design are intended for use by Proof to Partner. Do not misuse the website, interfere with its operation, attempt unauthorised access, harvest information or submit automated abusive traffic.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">8. Limitation and applicable law</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">These draft terms do not attempt to exclude or limit a liability or right that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited. The final version requires jurisdiction-specific review and a clause identifying applicable law and forum. This section is intentionally incomplete rather than asserting a jurisdiction that has not been provided.</p></section>
<section><h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">9. Contact and updates</h2><p class="prose-copy mt-3">Questions about these terms can be submitted through the <a class="font-semibold text-brand-deep underline" href="/contact/">contact page</a>. Monitor those enquiries and update the revision date whenever a substantive change is made.</p></section>
</article></section>
</SiteLayout>